Steps to Obtain Your Google Client ID
Go to the Google Cloud Console
Navigate to the Google Cloud Console in your web browser. Sign in with your Google account.
Select or Create a Project
From the project selector dashboard, select an existing project or create a new one for your iOS application.
Configure the OAuth Consent Screen
If you haven't done so already, you need to configure the consent screen. This is the prompt users will see asking for permission to access their information.
In the left-hand menu, go to APIs & Services > OAuth consent screen.
Select the User type (usually External for a public app) and click Create.
Fill in the required app information (app name, user support email, etc.) and save your changes. You can leave the "Scopes" and "Test users" sections with default values for now.
Create OAuth Client ID Credentials
In the left-hand menu, go to APIs & Services > Credentials.
Click the + CREATE CREDENTIALS button and select OAuth client ID.
Under Application type, select iOS.
Enter a Name for your OAuth client ID (this is just for your reference in the console).
Enter your app's Bundle ID (e.g., com.yourcompany.yourappname) exactly as it appears in your Xcode project's Info.plist file.
(Optional) You can also enter your App Store ID and Team ID if you have them, which are required for features like App Check.
Click Create.
Retrieve the Client ID
Your new OAuth client ID will be displayed. Copy this Client ID string. This is the value you will use to configure Google Sign-In within your iOS app's Xcode project. 
